#000\">mydf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_density</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>I am plotting densities for 2 groups of unequal size.</div><div>The first plot, without weights, creates densities with equal total weight for both groups.</div><div>The second and third plot do not do this.</div><div><br></div><div>Of course, it is possible to compute adjusted weights normalizing the sum for both groups,</div><div>but it would be better if there were a way of forcing equal total weights when plotting densities for multiple groups.</div><div>Can this be done?</div></div>"
